comments.body:
@fancycode any idea what would need to be done on our end?
CoTurn seems to support it:
> TLS (per RFC 5766 and RFC 6062): TLS1.0/TLS1.1/TLS1.2; ECDHE is supported.

@plinss 
If I understood [the discussion in your PR](https://github.com/nextcloud/spreed/pull/4715#issuecomment-753997048) correctly, the ordering/prioritisation of multiple TURN server is outside of control of Nextcloud, but in the hands of the client software. So if no high performance backend is used, probably only a single TURN server can reasonably be used, a single TURNS server, if required. When a high performance backend is used, it can handle communication between TURN servers.

I still did not fully understand if/how multiple clients could share a call when connecting to different TURN severs (each getting a list and deciding client-side which one to pick), when no high performance backend is involved, or if e.g. Coturn can be configured communicate with other TURN servers. Let's make it an own issue, since this one is bloated with the question whether or not to implement TURNS support at all 👍.
